
---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy | Finavit Journal"
  description="Discover how Finavit Journal researches, writes, reviews, sources, and updates its nutrition and wellness articles."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">OUR EDITORIAL STANDARDS</span>
    <h1>Editorial <em>Policy.</em></h1>
    <p>
      Our approach to researching, writing, sourcing, and maintaining
      trustworthy nutrition and wellness information.
    </p>
    <span class="updated">Last updated: November 16, 2026</span>
  </section>

  <article class="content">
    <p class="intro">
      At Finavit Journal, we believe useful health and nutrition
      information should be clear, transparent, and grounded in
      credible evidence. This policy explains the standards we aim
      to follow when creating and maintaining our content.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Our Editorial Mission</h2>
    <p>
      Our mission is to make information about nutrition, food,
      vitamins, and everyday wellness easier to understand.
      We aim to help readers explore these subjects through
      accessible explanations and practical educational content.
    </p>

    <h2>2. Research and Sources</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to prioritize reliable sources when researching
      articles. Depending on the topic, these may include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Peer-reviewed scientific research and academic publications.</li>
      <li>Government health agencies and public health institutions.</li>
      <li>Recognized medical and scientific organizations.</li>
      <li>Universities and established research institutions.</li>
      <li>Official nutritional databases and scientific references.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We aim to link to relevant original research or authoritative
      references so readers can explore important claims further.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Accuracy and Fact-Checking</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to check factual claims against credible references
      before publication. We also strive to distinguish established
      scientific findings from preliminary research, uncertainty,
      and emerging evidence.
    </p>
    <p>
      Scientific understanding can change. We therefore cannot
      guarantee that every article will always be completely
      current or free from errors.
    </p>

    <h2>4. Writing and Readability</h2>
    <p>
      Our content is written to make complex subjects easier to
      understand without unnecessarily oversimplifying important
      scientific details.
    </p>
    <p>
      We aim to use clear language, meaningful headings, practical
      explanations, and references where appropriate.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Use of Artificial Intelligence</h2>
    <p>
      Artificial intelligence may be used as an editorial
      assistance tool during research, drafting, organization,
      or content development.
    </p>
    <p>
      AI-generated material can contain inaccurate or misleading
      information. We aim to review and verify factual claims
      against credible sources before publication. AI tools do
      not replace scientific evidence or qualified professional
      judgment.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Updates and Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      We aim to review published articles when relevant scientific
      guidance changes, important new evidence becomes available,
      or an error is identified.
    </p>
    <p>
      When an article is substantially updated, we may display
      an updated publication date or an explanation of the change.
    </p>
    <p>
      Readers who identify a possible factual error are encouraged
      to contact us so we can review it.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Independence and Transparency</h2>
    <p>
      Our goal is to provide useful information without misleading
      readers or presenting commercial interests as scientific
      conclusions.
    </p>
    <p>
      If we introduce sponsored content, affiliate relationships,
      or other commercial arrangements, we aim to disclose them
      clearly where applicable.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Medical and Health Limitations</h2>
    <p>
      Finavit Journal publishes educational content, not
      individualized medical advice. Our articles are not a
      substitute for consultation with qualified healthcare
      professionals.
    </p>
    <p>
      For more information, please read our
      <a href="/blog/disclaimer/">Health Disclaimer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Contact the Editorial Team</h2>
    <p>
      Have a correction, question, or suggestion about one of
      our articles? We welcome reader feedback.
    </p>
    <p class="contact">
      <strong>Email:</strong>
      <a href="mailto:privacy@finavit.com">privacy@finavit.com</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .hero {
    padding: 85px 24px 65px;
    text-align: center;
    background: #f0f2e9;
  }

  .eyebrow {
    color: #68806d;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 2px;
  }

  .hero h1 {
    margin: 22px 0 14px;
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(42px, 7vw, 66px);
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .hero h1 em {
    color: #52745a;
  }

  .hero p {
    max-width: 620px;
    margin: auto;
    color: #68736a;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .updated {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 22px;
    color: #849087;
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .content {
    max-width: 790px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 65px 24px 85px;
  }

  .content h2 {
    margin: 42px 0 13px;
    font-family: 'DM Serif Display', serif;
    font-size: 25px;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .content p,
  .content li {
    color: #68736a;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.95;
  }

  .content ul {
    padding-left: 24px;
  }

  .content li {
    padding: 3px 0;
  }

  .intro {
    font-size: 16px !important;
  }

  .content a {
    color: #315e42;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .contact {
    padding: 16px 20px;
    border: 1px solid #e5e8df;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: #fdfdf9;
  }
</style>
